<article class="env-definition" id="0C7H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C7H">Definition <span data-tag="0C7H">55.4.1</span>.</a> Let $n, m_ i, a_{ij}, w_ i, g_ i$ be a numerical type $T$. The <em>Picard group of $T$</em> is the cokernel of the matrix $(a_{ij}/w_ i)$, more precisely </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (T) = \mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}\left( \mathbf{Z}^{\oplus n} \to \mathbf{Z}^{\oplus n},\quad e_ i \mapsto \sum \frac{a_{ij}}{w_ j}e_ j \right)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $e_ i$ denotes the $i$th standard basis vector for $\mathbf{Z}^{\oplus n}$. </p>
</article>